Testing that `option dns` on an interface is read, not just `list dns`.

A dns_policy whose dest_dns names an interface takes that interface's servers
from uci, `network.<iface>.dns`. uci returns a LIST option as an array and a
plain option as one whitespace-separated string, and both forms are ordinary
things to find in /etc/config/network:

	option dns '10.9.0.1 fd00::9'      -> "10.9.0.1 fd00::9"   (string)
	list dns '10.9.0.1'                -> [ "10.9.0.1", ... ]  (array)

Only the array form was handled. The string went into is_ipv4()/is_ipv6()
whole, matched neither, and both servers were dropped -- the policy then had no
address for either family and emitted nothing.

Both fixtures below carry the SAME two servers, written the two ways. They
must produce the same rules.

